From 0d279d55995fe295a96c8c0671b49e4c321d27ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hoangvu12 <hggaming91@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 14:06:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] zgx: a send not delivered can be discarded, and sent again
 whole
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A prompt that failed before its run was made (a file's upload failed, the
link to the chat's device was down, a new chat not yet known here) had no
run to send again, so "Not delivered — send again" dropped its row: the
composer was said to have the words, but a new chat's had already let them
go, so the message was gone (Discord, 2026-11-24: a new chat on another
device, sent while the link to it dropped for 5 s). And a failed row could
only be sent again: one that kept failing (a file over the 24 MB a message
may carry) sat under every later turn until Zeron restarted.

A pending prompt now keeps the send as it was asked for, and one with no run
is sent again whole from it under its own id, its row staying meanwhile.
Its row says why when that's known ("A file is over 24 MB"), and offers
Discard (`chat.discard`): the row goes and it's never sent; one still in
the engine's outbox is taken out of it first (RemoveHeldSend, by the id
follow_held now keeps). Only a failed row can be discarded. Preview mode
refuses it, as it does chat.retry. Zeron v2's lane_tab copy passes it too.

Tests: chat_pending_tests' a_send_that_failed_before_its_run_is_sent_again_
whole_not_dropped and discard_lets_a_failed_prompt_go_but_never_one_on_its_
way; chat_in_place's Discard and too-large lines (chat_fixture's
`undelivered_too_large`, and `discard` stubbed).
